From 0a8f3ba3f0e91b41667ee2f4748007c8e1a38321 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:10:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0267 -- the RTC pump is opt-in
 (SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_WB_RTC_PUMP=1)

Until now kind 3 was the default for any WaveBlaster on the paced
direct-port transport (the 320 us TX delay), with
SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_WB_RTC_PUMP=0 as a killswitch. The player asks for kind
3 whenever kind 2 is refused, so any WB setup without the blind overrides
got the pump without asking.

The pump has been measured on one card only: the PicoGUS firmware MPU
feeding a DreamBlaster S2 (dosags WBF1/WBF2 passed the on-time gate there,
with SDL 0265), in cells that forced the paced transport. The case it
exists for, a Creative MPU UART feeding the header (the Vibra16S lane), is
untested. A transport that owns IRQ 8 and services BIOS waits must not
reach an untested setup by default.

So Enable(3) now refuses unless SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_WB_RTC_PUMP=1 (strict
"1"), and the port keeps its main-loop poll as before 0260. Nothing else
changes:
- with the hint, the pump behaves exactly as without this patch;
- OPL3 (kind 1) and the blind MPU replay (kind 2) never reach this check;
- the poll path is what a refused kind 3 always fell back to.
Revisit the default after the Vibra16S cells.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nz9XeKeVG8Ab7dm8esJsMu
---
 include/SDL3/SDL_dosmidi_tick.h |  5 +++--
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 10 ++++++----
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/SDL3/SDL_dosmidi_tick.h b/include/SDL3/SDL_dosmidi_tick.h
index 475994ed7..829b12735 100644
--- a/include/SDL3/SDL_dosmidi_tick.h
+++ b/include/SDL3/SDL_dosmidi_tick.h
@@ -317,8 +317,9 @@ extern SDL_DECLSPEC Uint32 SDLCALL SDL_DOSMidiDeferKeysOn(void);
    tick (IRQ 8, 2048 Hz), never closer than the transport's byte spacing. The
    PIT is not touched (uclock() unaffected). While enabled the pump owns IRQ 8
    and services the AT BIOS INT 15h/86h wait (DJGPP delay(), SDL_Delay) itself.
-   Enable(3) returns false for any other transport, when the killswitch
-   SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_WB_RTC_PUMP=0 is set, or while a BIOS wait is in progress.
+   Enable(3) returns false for any other transport, unless SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_WB_RTC_PUMP=1
+   opts in (patch 0267; before it, "0" was a killswitch and the pump the default), or while
+   a BIOS wait is in progress.
    Stats (run totals; rate and spacing of the last install, 0 if never
    installed): the pump's rate, byte spacing, RTC ticks taken, BIOS waits
    completed, and the longest release-to-write of an on-time byte in us (+- one
diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 4874c07f2..384921878 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -2893,12 +2893,14 @@ bool SDL_DOSMidiDeferEnable(int kind)
     }
     if (kind == 3) {
         /* DOS-PORT patch 0260: the TIMED-DELAY transport, paced by the RTC pump.
-           Killswitch SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_WB_RTC_PUMP=0 (strict "0"): refused, so
-           the port keeps its main-loop poll. */
+           DOS-PORT patch 0267: opt-in. Only SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_WB_RTC_PUMP=1 (strict "1")
+           enables it; otherwise kind 3 is refused and the port keeps its main-loop poll. The
+           pump is measured only on one card (PicoGUS + DreamBlaster, with the hint's effect
+           forced); an untested header must not get it by default. */
         const char *h = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_WB_RTC_PUMP");
         Uint32 gap_us = 0;
-        if (h && h[0] == '0' && h[1] == 0) {
-            dos_port_dbg_log("audio: patch 0260 RTC pump off (SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_WB_RTC_PUMP=0)");
+        if (!(h && h[0] == '1' && h[1] == 0)) {
+            dos_port_dbg_log("audio: patch 0267 RTC pump not enabled (opt-in: SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_WB_RTC_PUMP=1)");
             return false;
         }
         if (!SDL_DOSMpu401PacedDirectBase(&g_mdq_mpu_base, &gap_us)) {
-- 
